    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-6161",
      "problem": "Determine the intervals in which the function $y= f(x)$ below is continuous. You may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14262965/assets/8281f79b06b2fa551d1a0a11135d749ba3bfbee0127c677288e90991b9aebf78.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The function is continuous on the open intervals $(-\\infty,-1),$ $(-1,1)$ and $(1,\\infty).$\n\nAdditionally, the function is right-continuous at $x=-1.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $[-1,1).$\n\nTherefore, we can say that the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty,-1),$ $[-1,1)$ and $(1,\\infty).$ It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals.",
